{%- comment -%}
  GPSR Article 19 — product safety information in the online offer.

  Regulation (EU) 2023/988 requires that an online offer of a product carries,
  in the offer itself, the manufacturer's name and postal and electronic
  address; where the manufacturer is outside the EU, the details of the EU
  responsible person; product identification including type, batch or serial
  number; and any warnings or safety information, in a language the consumer
  easily understands.

  Three implementation notes that matter:

  1. Footer or terms-page placement does not satisfy this. The information must
     be on, or one click from, the product page.

  2. The local-language requirement means Dutch for NL, German for DE, and
     French as well as Dutch for Belgium. These are translatable metafields,
     not theme settings — the content differs per product AND per market.

  3. A SET IS NOT ONE PRODUCT. The starter set is a single Shopify product but
     several physical products, possibly from different factories. Article 19
     applies to each of them, so `compliance.component_details` renders
     per-component information when a set is being sold. Rendering one
     manufacturer block for a three-component set would be wrong.

  FAIL-CLOSED BEHAVIOUR: when the required data is absent this snippet renders a
  customer-visible notice, and `main-product.liquid` disables the add-to-cart
  button. An earlier version showed the warning only in the theme editor, which
  meant a live product with empty metafields displayed nothing at all and failed
  silently — precisely the outcome the design was supposed to prevent.

  Source: research/eu-compliance-constraints.md §2.3 and
  operations/gpsr-runbook.md. Secondary sources only; the primary text could not
  be opened from the build environment.
  REQUIRES PROFESSIONAL VERIFICATION before launch.

  Accepts: product
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign m = product.metafields.compliance
  assign has_single = false
  assign has_components = false

  if m.manufacturer_name != blank and m.manufacturer_address != blank
    assign has_single = true
  endif
  if m.component_details != blank
    assign has_components = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if has_components or has_single -%}
  <section class="regulatory" aria-labelledby="regulatory-heading-{{ product.id }}">
    <h2 id="regulatory-heading-{{ product.id }}" class="text-s">
      {{ 'product.regulatory.heading' | t }}
    </h2>

    {%- if has_components -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A set: each component carries its own manufacturer and identification.
        Maintained as rich text by operations rather than as separate metafields,
        because the component count varies per set.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rte">{{ m.component_details }}</div>
    {%- else -%}
      <dl>
        <dt>{{ 'product.regulatory.manufacturer' | t }}</dt>
        <dd>
          {{ m.manufacturer_name | escape }}<br>
          {{ m.manufacturer_address | escape | newline_to_br }}<br>
          {%- if m.manufacturer_email != blank -%}
            <a href="mailto:{{ m.manufacturer_email }}">{{ m.manufacturer_email }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </dd>

        {%- comment -%}
          Rendered only when the manufacturer is outside the EU. For this venture
          the merchant is usually the NL-established responsible person, so this
          block is normally empty — but the theme must support the other case or
          it cannot list a third-party product lawfully.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if m.responsible_person_name != blank -%}
          <dt>{{ 'product.regulatory.responsible_person' | t }}</dt>
          <dd>
            {{ m.responsible_person_name | escape }}<br>
            {{ m.responsible_person_address | escape | newline_to_br }}<br>
            {%- if m.responsible_person_email != blank -%}
              <a href="mailto:{{ m.responsible_person_email }}">{{ m.responsible_person_email }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </dd>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if m.product_identifier != blank -%}
          <dt>{{ 'product.regulatory.identification' | t }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ m.product_identifier | escape }}</dd>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if m.country_of_origin != blank -%}
          <dt>{{ 'product.regulatory.origin' | t }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ m.country_of_origin | escape }}</dd>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if m.materials != blank -%}
          <dt>{{ 'product.regulatory.materials' | t }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ m.materials | escape }}</dd>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if m.care_instructions != blank -%}
          <dt>{{ 'product.regulatory.care' | t }}</dt>
          <dd>{{ m.care_instructions | escape }}</dd>
        {%- endif -%}
      </dl>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if m.warnings != blank -%}
      <div role="note">
        <strong>{{ 'product.regulatory.warnings' | t }}</strong>
        <div>{{ m.warnings }}</div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>

{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Missing data. Two audiences, two messages.

    Customers see a plain, non-alarming notice explaining the product is
    unavailable — shown because the add-to-cart is disabled and an unexplained
    dead button is worse than an explained one.

    Staff additionally see exactly what is missing and where to fix it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="regulatory" role="status">
    <p>{{ 'product.regulatory.unavailable' | t }}</p>

    {%- if request.design_mode -%}
      <p>
        <strong>Staff: missing GPSR data for “{{ product.title }}”.</strong>
        This product cannot lawfully be offered in the EU, so purchase is
        disabled. Populate either <code>compliance.component_details</code> (for
        a multi-item set) or <code>compliance.manufacturer_name</code> plus
        <code>compliance.manufacturer_address</code> (for a single item).
        See <code>venture/operations/gpsr-runbook.md</code> §8.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>
{%- endif -%}
